infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Single-shard commit vs cross-shard 2PC
  desc Why co-location is the senior default for transactions
  compares
    - label Single-shard transaction
      children
        - label 1 round-trip
          desc Normal Postgres COMMIT on one node
        - label No 2PC
          desc Co-located tables, single-node atomicity
        - label No in-doubt risk
          desc Nothing left in pg_prepared_xacts
    - label Cross-shard 2PC
      children
        - label 2+ round-trips
          desc Prepare phase + commit phase = ~2x latency
        - label Lower throughput
          desc Each shard holds its connection open during prepare
        - label In-doubt risk
          desc Coordinator crash leaves prepared xacts holding locks
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
